70 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 252 0 R
/E (Over 450 million individuals are employed in India's informal labor market, and a sizable fraction of them are skilled people who work in maintenance, building, and home repair. The process by which a family finds a reliable, available plumber or electrician has not significantly changed in decades, despite this large workforce. The dominant model remains word-of-mouth referral or physical search which are inherently slow  , geographically constrained, and opaque.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
71 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 253 0 R
/E (Meanwhile, There are more than 700 million smartphone users in India and regional language apps make smartphones accessible to people who don't speak English. Although a digital labor marketplace's infrastructure is in place, its design has not been sufficiently adapted to the real user base.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
72 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 254 0 R
/E (Crewli positions itself at this intersection. It's not a platform for general gigs. It is a context-specific, trust-first, speed-optimized platform built around the realities of how unpaid skilled people work and how customers think when they have a power outage or a broken pipe at eight o'clock on a Saturday.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
